From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:28:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] proton: Add DXVK-Sarek fallback for GPUs current DXVK cannot
 drive.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DXVK requires storageBuffer8BitAccess, which Turnip exposes only on
Adreno 7xx and newer, so Adreno 650 gets no D3D adapter. Build
DXVK-Sarek alongside DXVK and select it when the primary GPU lacks
the required features, or with PROTON_DXVK_SAREK=1.

Ported from Proton-CachyOS: extras/build-dxvk-sarek.mk, vulkan.py, the
GPU probe from utilities.py, and the proton script hooks (Stelios
Tsampas, Katharina Dröge, loathingKernel). The probe also requires
storageBuffer8BitAccess, and the Sarek choice is part of the prefix
config so toggling it relinks the DLLs.

The probe imports lazily so a missing Vulkan loader keeps default DXVK,
and GPUs are grouped by type without itertools.groupby, which split
unsorted lists and could drop the matching device.
